    "text": "To determine Margaret's test score, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate Marco's test score.\n2. Use Marco's score to find Margaret's score.\n\nFirst, we know the average score on the test was 90. Marco scored 10% less than the average. To find Marco's score, we calculate 10% of 90 and subtract it from 90:\n\n\\[ 10\\% \\text{ of } 90 = 0.10 \\times 90 = 9 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Marco's score} = 90 - 9 = 81 \\]\n\nNext, we know that Margaret received 5 more points than Marco. So, we add 5 to Marco's score to find Margaret's score:\n\n\\[ \\text{Margaret's score} = 81 + 5 = 86 \\]\n\nTherefore, Margaret's score on her test is \\(\\boxed{86}\\).",
